# .gitignore for the budget app — ASP.NET Core + Rider + SQLite
# Drop this in the repo root next to budget-app-spec.md, before the first commit.
# It exists so no secret, token, spreadsheet ID, or local financial data
# ever lands on GitHub (spec §2, §13: "No secret, token, or spreadsheet ID
# is committed to the repo").

## .NET build outputs
bin/
obj/
out/
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb

## Rider / JetBrains
.idea/
*.sln.iml

## Visual Studio (if you ever open it there)
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

## Local database — contains your real budget data, never commit it
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

## Secrets and credentials — use dotnet user-secrets / env vars instead (spec §2)
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.*.json
!appsettings.json
*.pfx
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
token.json
*.env
.env
secrets.json

## OS / misc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
